      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a creative agency, you need language that speaks to *flow* and *creative momentum*, not just spreadsheets. You can frame this as a disruption to the established rhythm, like a misplaced, unpredictable element in a carefully crafted piece of work. Instead of \"chaos,\" try describing it as an **\"intermittent friction point\"** in the team's established creative flow.\n\nA more character-driven metaphor might be comparing it to a **\"recurring, minor impedance to forward momentum.\"** This suggests the lateness isn't a massive roadblock, but a persistent, irritating snag—like a single, slightly bent piece of wire in an otherwise perfect circuit. It acknowledges the brilliance while pointing to the subtle, persistent derailment.",
